By Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, 
\begin{align*}
\frac{a^2}{a+b}+\frac{b^2}{b+c}+\frac{c^2}{c+a}&=\frac{a^2}{a+b}\cdot 1+\frac{b^2}{b+c}\cdot 1+\frac{c^2}{c+a}\cdot 1\\
&\le\left(\frac{a^2}{a+b}+\frac{b^2}{b+c}+\frac{c^2}{c+a}\right)\left(1+1+1\right)\\
&=\left(a+b+c\right)\left(\frac{a}{a+b}+\frac{b}{b+c}+\frac{c}{c+a}\right)\\
&=1\cdot \left(\frac{a}{a+b}+\frac{b}{b+c}+\frac{c}{c+a}\right)
\end{align*}

By Cauchy-Schwarz inequality again, 
\begin{align*}
\left(\frac{a}{a+b}+\frac{b}{b+c}+\frac{c}{c+a}\right)\left(a+b+b+c+c+a\right)&\ge \left(\sqrt{\frac{a}{a+b}\cdot a}+\sqrt{\frac{b}{b+c}\cdot b}+\sqrt{\frac{c}{c+a}\cdot c}\right)^2\\
&=\left(\sqrt{a}+\sqrt{b}+\sqrt{c}\right)^2
\end{align*}

Therefore,
\begin{align*}
\frac{a^2}{a+b}+\frac{b^2}{b+c}+\frac{c^2}{c+a}&\le \left(\frac{a}{a+b}+\frac{b}{b+c}+\frac{c}{c+a}\right)\\
&\le \frac{\left(\sqrt{a}+\sqrt{b}+\sqrt{c}\right)^2}{2(a+b+c)}\\
&=\frac{\left(\sqrt{a}+\sqrt{b}+\sqrt{c}\right)^2}{2}
\end{align*}

It is known that $\left(\sqrt{a}+\sqrt{b}+\sqrt{c}\right)^2\le \left(\sqrt{3}\right)^2=3$, with equality when $a=b=c$. Hence, $\frac{a^2}{a+b}+\frac{b^2}{b+c}+\frac{c^2}{c+a}\le \frac{3}{2}$, with equality when $a=b=c=\frac{1}{3}$. Therefore, the maximum value is $\boxed{\frac{1}{2}}

